1180" y="622" class="td">368.42</text><line class="line" x1="48" y1="639" x2="1392" y2="639"/><text x="70" y="666" class="tdb">100</text><text x="245" y="666" class="td">10 (9.86 MB)</text><text x="515" y="666" class="td">479</text><text x="610" y="666" class="td">22</text><rect class="warn" x="710" y="646" width="94" height="28" rx="14"/><text x="757" y="665" text-anchor="middle" class="warnt">95.61%</text><text x="895" y="666" class="td">332.61</text><text x="1180" y="666" class="td">405.94</text><text x="28" y="738" class="st">RESULT ASSESSMENT</text><rect class="c" x="28" y="754" width="680" height="174" rx="13"/><text x="50" y="788" class="h3">Load Behaviour</text><text x="50" y="816" class="b">• All 10-user executions achieved 100% passing across the full 1-to-10-file range.</text><text x="50" y="840" class="b">• At 25 users, passing rates ranged from 93.04% to 100%; the 5-file run had the lowest rate.</text><text x="50" y="864" class="b">• The 50-user / 10-file run achieved 100% passing with 265.35 sec average and 368.42 sec P95.</text><text x="50" y="888" class="b">• At 100 users / 10 files, 22 failures reduced passing to 95.61%; average response time rose to 332.61 sec.</text><text x="50" y="912" class="b">• Highest P95 was 423.86 sec at 25 users / 10 files; the 100-user P95 was 405.94 sec.</text><rect class="c" x="732" y="754" width="680" height="174" rx="13"/><text x="754" y="788" class="h3">Management Assessment</text><text x="754" y="816" class="b">The latest DEV results extend validation to 50 and 100 concurrent users on the</text><text x="754" y="838" class="b">10-file workload. The 50-user execution completed without failure and with latency</text><text x="754" y="860" class="b">comparable to the 10-user / 10-file run. At 100 users, reliability degraded to</text><text x="754" y="882" class="b">95.61% passing and average response time increased to 332.61 sec. Results therefore</text><text x="754" y="904" class="b">show that 50-user / 10-file execution was stable in this run, while 100-user</text><text x="754" y="924" class="b">concurrency requires further reliability and latency validation.</text><text x="1412" y="958" text-anchor="end" class="s">Agent Hub Performance Testing • SOW Execution Result - DEV • 1 Sep 2026 • Management View</text></svg>